## SQ-ST-01 | swap files load: the load line counts the two waystone swaps, no bad entry
@group A
@commands boot; grep `[template-swaps]` in latest.log
@pass `[template-swaps] N block swap(s) in M template(s)` with N and M each 2 above the last run's line (1412 in 105 on 2026-10-30, before later swap changes); no `bad entry`, no `could not read`
@fails `TemplateBlockSwaps.CONFIGS` lacks `misc_block_swaps.json`; the file not in the server's `kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/`
bootexpect \[template-swaps\] \d+ block swap\(s\) in \d+ template\(s\)
bootreject \[template-swaps\] .*(bad entry|could not read)

## SQ-ST-02 | the placed village waystones (common and desert) have yellow corundum at [2, 0, 3], not glowstone
@phase worldgen
@group A
@commands `forceload add 700 700 740 740`; `/place template waystones:village/common/waystone 700 -60 700`; `/place template waystones:village/desert/waystone 720 -60 700`; `execute if block 702 -60 703 quark:yellow_corundum`; the same at 722 -60 703; grep the log for `no longer hold`
@pass both positions hold `quark:yellow_corundum`; no glowstone in either piece; no `no longer hold` warning naming a waystones template
@fails position or `from` wrong in `misc_block_swaps.json` (template changed in Waystones 11.4.2): warning `marked position(s) no longer hold their block`
> forceload add 700 700 740 740
> place template waystones:village/common/waystone 700 -60 700
> place template waystones:village/desert/waystone 720 -60 700
> execute if block 702 -60 703 quark:yellow_corundum run say ST02-common
> execute if block 722 -60 703 quark:yellow_corundum run say ST02-desert
> cdevtest count 700 -60 700 712 -50 712 minecraft:glowstone
> cdevtest count 720 -60 700 732 -50 712 minecraft:glowstone
expect ST02-common$
expect ST02-desert$
reject \[template-swaps\] waystones:\S+: \d+ marked position
look both say lines; glowstone count n=0 in both boxes
